{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Let Pharaoh do.</b> The intention of the words is that Yoseph understood that the reason for the dream is that HaShem is bringing seven years of plenty with abundance greater than the other years, so that the produce may serve as supply for the seven years of famine. And without the dream being made known, when the harvest of the first year arrives abundant, then when the second year comes the sowers of grain will slacken off, for they will say: ״Look — the first year's harvest has produced enough for three years.״ And also on account of the abundance, grain will be cheap and they will slacken from the labor of plowing and sowing and their preparations; and also the sowers in the second year, when they see it blessed, will further slacken from sowing more — and all the more so after three or four years have passed, they will do no work in the field to sow or to plow. Therefore Elohim made known that what He gives in greater measure in these years is for the sustenance of the seven years of famine, and therefore he said to Pharaoh, <b>Let Pharaoh do and appoint</b> etc. — meaning that he himself should devote himself to this matter and also cause others to do it, so that no person should slacken in this matter of preparing during the seven years of plenty, to sow with all possible capability." "<b>And let him take a fifth</b> — meaning, he should spur them on so as not to slacken, because of seeing the matter [produce] greatly multiplied. Or it may say <b>and let him take a fifth</b> — that he should take from all of them a fifth for Pharaoh, even though the law is a tithe (I Samuel 8:17); in these years he should take a fifth, as payment for the matter being made known through him, and also because he does kindness with them: all the grain that becomes Pharaoh's — he will lay no hand upon it, but it will stand ready for their sustenance, to sell it to them in the years of famine, as it says: ״וְהָיָה הָאֹכֶל לְפִקָּדוֹן״. In this he hinted at what we have written — that he would lay no hand upon it, and also that he would not sell from the grain to others during the years of famine until they had first come to purchase their needs; as I shall explain in the verse that follows this one."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:42.382616218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}